# pyenv
#   For a library or app, you might want to commit .python-version.
#   However, if you're using uv, it's optional. Let's allow it or exclude.
# .python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#598, it is recommended to include Pipfile.lock in git.
#   However, on standalone applications, it can be useful.
#Pipfile.lock

# poetry
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, it is generally recommended to include poetry.lock in git.
#poetry.lock

# pdm
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, it is generally recommended to include pdm.lock in git.
#pdm.lock

# PEP 582; project packages directory (used by pdm)
